    "q-43403": {
      "dom_id": "step-q43403",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "What is the period of the function $f(x)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})?$",
      "worked_solution": "Given a function in the form $y=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=3.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$",
