    "q-236902": {
      "dom_id": "step-q236902",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the equation of the midline for a transformed cosine function with a minimum value of $-13$ and a maximum value of $-1.$",
      "worked_solution": "A sinusoidal graph's midline (or vertical shift) is the horizontal line that divides it vertically in half. \n\nThe equation of the midline is given by\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{\\text{min}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{max}}$ are the minimum and maximum values of the function. The midline equals the average of the maximum and minimum values. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2} & =\\frac{-13+(-1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-14}{2} \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the midline is $y=-7.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
