    "q-25513": {
      "dom_id": "step-q25513",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "What is the range of the function $f(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x+\\pi )-2?$",
      "worked_solution": "The range of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x+\\pi )\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-1$ and then subtracting $2$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x+\\pi )\\le 1 \\\\  & 1\\ge -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x+\\pi )\\ge -1 \\\\  & -1\\ge \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x+\\pi )-2\\ge -3 \\\\  & -3\\le f(x)\\le -1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)\\in [-3,-1].$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
