    "q-40967": {
      "dom_id": "step-q40967",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Find the range of the function $f(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-3.$",
      "worked_solution": "The range of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $2$ and then subtracting $3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\le 1 \\\\  & -2\\le 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\le 2 \\\\  & -5\\le 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-3\\le -1 \\\\  & -5\\le f(x)\\le -1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)\\in [-5,-1].$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
